window.MAPS = [{"id":"drezen","order":1,"title":"Drezen","subtitle":"The liberated citadel-city on the Ahari. The company's base, and the ground of the real work.","image":"images/map-drezen-city.webp","scale":"the walls to the South Bank, a little under a mile","surface":null,"hexes":null,"intro":"Seventy-five years of demon rule, and then the walls came back into crusade hands on the **13th\nof Rova, 4713**. What the chart shows is a city relearning how to be one: the citadel and its\ncurtain wall holding the high ground, two compounds gone up on the eastern ridge, a market\ncrowded against the gate, and a whole quarter across the dry Ahari that nobody has searched,\nbecause searching it would mean going in. North is to the upper right. The cemetery is to the\nleft, and growing.","places":[{"id":"citadel-drezen","name":"Citadel Drezen","x":38.6,"y":29.8,"kind":"city","style":"pin","letter":"A","revealed":true,"chapter":"","chapterId":"","chapterLabel":"","md":"The star-fort in its moat, inside a pentagonal curtain wall with six towers and one gate facing\nsouth into the city. The crusade holds it outright, and the garrison lives here, behind the\nwalls, where the crusade has always preferred to be. Everything the company is paid to do is\ncounted out of this arch and counted back through it. The ledger at the gate has three columns:\n*Out*, *In*, and *Shrinkage*. It is the most complete record Drezen keeps.","text":"Citadel Drezen The star-fort in its moat, inside a pentagonal curtain wall with six towers and one gate facing south into the city. The crusade holds it outright, and the garrison lives here, behind the walls, where the crusade has always preferred to be. Everything the company is paid to do is counted out of this arch and counted back through it. The ledger at the gate has three columns: Out , In , and Shrinkage . It is the most complete record Drezen keeps."},{"id":"iomedae-s-preservers","name":"Iomedae's Preservers","x":74.8,"y":16.2,"kind":"city","style":"pin","letter":"B","revealed":true,"chapter":"","chapterId":"","chapterLabel":"","md":"**Harlock Greyforge's** order, walled on the high ground north-east of the city: garrison,\nbarracks, chapel, stable, a watchtower over the western approach, and a parade ground drilled\nevery morning by people who are not yet sure what they are drilling for. Five squads to hold a\ncity, and their commander days out of contact in the west. **Elara Dawnstrider** calls the\nrecruits and runs the three-day trial. Her account of it: \"The first day tells me if you can\nstand. The second tells me if you can stand it. The third is for the ones I'm keeping, so they\ncan eat.\"","text":"Iomedae's Preservers Harlock Greyforge's order, walled on the high ground north-east of the city: garrison, barracks, chapel, stable, a watchtower over the western approach, and a parade ground drilled every morning by people who are not yet sure what they are drilling for. Five squads to hold a city, and their commander days out of contact in the west. Elara Dawnstrider calls the recruits and runs the three-day trial. Her account of it: \"The first day tells me if you can stand. The second tells me if you can stand it. The third is for the ones I'm keeping, so they can eat.\""},{"id":"varic-s-temple-compound","name":"Varic's Temple Compound","x":66.4,"y":37.2,"kind":"temple","style":"pin","letter":"C","revealed":true,"chapter":"","chapterId":"","chapterLabel":"","md":"**Varic Sarian's** foundation on the eastern ridge, ringed by its own low wall, because even the\nDawnflower's people have noticed where they are. The **Temple of Sarenrae** stands at the centre\nwith the **temple of the united faiths**, **Sosiel Vaenic's**, across the way from it. Asked how\nthe gods were getting along under one roof, Sosiel said, \"Better than their priests. I've had to\nmove the pews twice.\" An orphanage, a food bank and an infirmary fill the rest of the ground,\nwhich says plainly what the compound is for, and what the city is producing.","text":"Varic's Temple Compound Varic Sarian's foundation on the eastern ridge, ringed by its own low wall, because even the Dawnflower's people have noticed where they are. The Temple of Sarenrae stands at the centre with the temple of the united faiths , Sosiel Vaenic's , across the way from it. Asked how the gods were getting along under one roof, Sosiel said, \"Better than their priests. I've had to move the pews twice.\" An orphanage, a food bank and an infirmary fill the rest of the ground, which says plainly what the compound is for, and what the city is producing."},{"id":"rabiah-s-compound","name":"Rabiah's Compound","x":80.8,"y":38.3,"kind":"site","style":"pin","letter":"D","revealed":true,"chapter":"","chapterId":"","chapterLabel":"","md":"The ring quarter east of the ridge: bazaar, brewery, bathhouse, community kitchen, workshop row\nand a shrine over a meeting square, wound in circles around the old amphitheatre. Built fast and\nbuilt crooked. The kitchen and the dining hall were begun from two ends by two people and met at\nthe wrong angle, and the result is known throughout Drezen as **Tuesday's mistake**. Wednesday,\nthey started over there. **Tilda Merrow**, an aging adept, keeps the compound from dying of its\nown enthusiasm, and describes her duties as \"splints, soup, and saying no.\" **Sir Brannic\nVayne** keeps the lists. He is not really a knight. He has beautiful handwriting, and a seal, and\nhas never confirmed or denied which came first.","text":"Rabiah's Compound The ring quarter east of the ridge: bazaar, brewery, bathhouse, community kitchen, workshop row and a shrine over a meeting square, wound in circles around the old amphitheatre. Built fast and built crooked. The kitchen and the dining hall were begun from two ends by two people and met at the wrong angle, and the result is known throughout Drezen as Tuesday's mistake . Wednesday, they started over there. Tilda Merrow , an aging adept, keeps the compound from dying of its own enthusiasm, and describes her duties as \"splints, soup, and saying no.\" Sir Brannic Vayne keeps the lists. He is not really a knight. He has beautiful handwriting, and a seal, and has never confirmed or denied which came first."},{"id":"the-amphitheatre","name":"The Amphitheatre","x":81.1,"y":33.8,"kind":"ruin","style":"icon","letter":"","revealed":true,"chapter":"","chapterId":"","chapterLabel":"","md":"Pre-crusade stone at the heart of Rabiah's quarter, cleared and back in use. The one place in the\ncity that will hold a crowd, which nobody has yet had a reason to test.","text":"The Amphitheatre Pre-crusade stone at the heart of Rabiah's quarter, cleared and back in use. The one place in the city that will hold a crowd, which nobody has yet had a reason to test."},{"id":"celeste-market-district","name":"Celeste Market District","x":52.1,"y":54.2,"kind":"site","style":"pin","letter":"E","revealed":true,"chapter":"","chapterId":"","chapterLabel":"","md":"**Lupenor Celest's** foundation, packed between the citadel wall and the riverbank: street\nvendors under canvas, an auction house, warehouses along the wall, three inns and **Lupenor's\nresidence** above it all, where the money can be watched. **Mira Thistledance** screens the\ntraders who work here. Asked her criteria, she said, \"Yes.\" **Silas Thorne** sells cloth, in a\ncity where everyone's clothes are ruined, and is doing very well. **Abner Suthi** trades honey\nand sweets; he once died on a spike above a lava lake and was brought back, and he sells sweets,\nand he has thought about it. From the board outside the auction house, this week:\n\n> *ROPE, new, Kenabres: 4 sp the fathom.*\\\n> *ROPE, used, South Bank: ask.*\\\n> *HONEY, Suthi's: 2 sp the jar. Sweets: 1 cp, or a story he hasn't heard.*\\\n> *CLOTH, Thorne's: whatever you have. He will make it work.*\\\n> *WANTED: persons of no company for a job of no description. Office above. Knock once.*\n\nThe company's first employer keeps that office.","text":"Celeste Market District Lupenor Celest's foundation, packed between the citadel wall and the riverbank: street vendors under canvas, an auction house, warehouses along the wall, three inns and Lupenor's residence above it all, where the money can be watched. Mira Thistledance screens the traders who work here. Asked her criteria, she said, \"Yes.\" Silas Thorne sells cloth, in a city where everyone's clothes are ruined, and is doing very well. Abner Suthi trades honey and sweets; he once died on a spike above a lava lake and was brought back, and he sells sweets, and he has thought about it. From the board outside the auction house, this week: ROPE, new, Kenabres: 4 sp the fathom. ROPE, used, South Bank: ask. HONEY, Suthi's: 2 sp the jar. Sweets: 1 cp, or a story he hasn't heard. CLOTH, Thorne's: whatever you have. He will make it work. WANTED: persons of no company for a job of no description. Office above. Knock once. The company's first employer keeps that office."},{"id":"the-ahari-riverbed","name":"The Ahari Riverbed","x":44.9,"y":65.4,"kind":"water","style":"pin","letter":"","revealed":true,"chapter":"","chapterId":"","chapterLabel":"","md":"The river ran out of its bed when the Worldwound opened and never came back. What is left is a\ndry channel cutting the city in half, crossed by two bridges, and a road for anything that would\nrather not use the gates. A great many things would rather not.","text":"The Ahari Riverbed The river ran out of its bed when the Worldwound opened and never came back. What is left is a dry channel cutting the city in half, crossed by two bridges, and a road for anything that would rather not use the gates. A great many things would rather not."},{"id":"south-bank","name":"South Bank","x":53.9,"y":81.8,"kind":"ruin","style":"pin","letter":"F","revealed":true,"chapter":"","chapterId":"","chapterLabel":"","md":"The quarter across the riverbed: scrap yards and rope-walks that spent seventy-five years under\ndemon rule and have not been searched. **Cinder Row** runs through it. The crusade holds the\nwalls above it and very little of what is under its roofs, and has decided that this counts.\nThis is where the work is. This is why the company is being paid, and why the pay is what it is.","text":"South Bank The quarter across the riverbed: scrap yards and rope-walks that spent seventy-five years under demon rule and have not been searched. Cinder Row runs through it. The crusade holds the walls above it and very little of what is under its roofs, and has decided that this counts. This is where the work is. This is why the company is being paid, and why the pay is what it is."},{"id":"the-cemetery","name":"The Cemetery","x":7.2,"y":75.7,"kind":"site","style":"icon","letter":"","revealed":true,"chapter":"","chapterId":"","chapterLabel":"","md":"Outside the walls to the west, on the far bank. Older than the occupation, and added to steadily\nsince the retaking. The only district in Drezen with a growing population.","text":"The Cemetery Outside the walls to the west, on the far bank. Older than the occupation, and added to steadily since the retaking. The only district in Drezen with a growing population."},{"id":"the-western-road","name":"The Western Road","x":3.0,"y":46.0,"kind":"region","style":"pin","letter":"","revealed":true,"chapter":"","chapterId":"","chapterLabel":"","md":"Out of the west gate and into the Marchlands: two days on foot to the **Sarian Fane**, with\nnothing on the road in between. \"Nothing\" is a technical term.","text":"The Western Road Out of the west gate and into the Marchlands: two days on foot to the Sarian Fane , with nothing on the road in between. \"Nothing\" is a technical term."}]}];